 "notes": "Manual: recall from two files read whole — the challenges REST namespace (CTFd/api/v1/challenges.py) and the auth blueprint (CTFd/auth.py). Flask blueprints without url_prefix (auth, views, admin, challenges) come out right, methods=[...] included. The REST API is flask-restx: @challenges_namespace.route(\"/<challenge_id>/solves\") on a Resource class whose methods are def get/post/patch/delete, the namespace added with CTFd_API_v1.add_namespace(ns, \"/challenges\") on a Blueprint with url_prefix=\"/api/v1\" — until 2026-10-16 the routes came out as GET without /api/v1/<namespace> and the other methods of each Resource were lost (restx-resource), and a namespace route that shadowed a blueprint one (GET /teams, /users) hid it. Since then each method of a Resource is a route under the namespace and the Api's blueprint prefix: 155 routes in 90 classes, the count an ast walk of CTFd/api gives. The themes commit their built, minified bundles (themes/*/static/assets/*.js): calls in them are right but duplicated, and two minified $.get-like calls became routes (build-artifact). Calls: CTFd.fetch(\"/api/v1/...\", {method}) with the full path written out — right; a method held in a local variable (let method = \"PATCH\") comes out ANY (method-variable). Since the v2 cheap fixes (2026-10-15): the committed bundles (themes/*/static/assets/*-<hash>.js) are left out, a method or a path held in a local variable (let method, target +=) is read, and $.get is a call.",
